{
  "_comment": [
    "The eudev service definition: the device manager, and how peinit starts it.",
    "",
    "Identity is SYSTEM with RequiredPrivileges cut to the three udevd cannot",
    "work without, each found by taking it away and watching what broke:",
    "",
    "  SeLoadDriverPrivilege        init_module is CAP_SYS_MODULE. Loading",
    "                               drivers is the job. It is also the privilege",
    "                               the PIP chapter names as the ceiling of every",
    "                               kernel guarantee; module signature enforcement",
    "                               is what keeps it from meaning more than 'load",
    "                               a module Peios built'.",
    "  SeTcbPrivilege               udevd hands each event to a worker, and",
    "                               announces each processed event to libudev",
    "                               listeners, by MULTICAST on the uevent netlink",
    "                               socket. The kernel gates that send on",
    "                               CAP_NET_ADMIN (af_netlink.c, NL_CFG_F_NONROOT_SEND",
    "                               is not set for NETLINK_KOBJECT_UEVENT), which",
    "                               KACS maps to SeTcbPrivilege. Inherent to udev's",
    "                               design -- systemd-udevd keeps CAP_NET_ADMIN for",
    "                               the same reason -- and the one that makes the",
    "                               device manager a TCB component here. Without",
    "                               it every worker dies with EPERM.",
    "  SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege  /dev/disk/by-uuid and every other stable",
    "                               name is a symlink. Without it the directories",
    "                               appear and stay empty.",
    "",
    "Everything else udevd touches is governed by descriptors, not privileges:",
    "the nodes and links under /dev by the SD prelude seeds, uevent replays by",
    "sysfs's unmanaged policy.",
    "",
    "Readiness is Alive (1). udevd has no readiness protocol. The coldplug in",
    "ExecStartPost is what makes that honest: peinit releases dependents only",
    "after post-hooks finish, and the hook does not return until udevd has",
    "answered its control socket, the enumeration has been replayed, and the",
    "queue has drained. A service that Requires eudev therefore starts with",
    "the devices present at boot already handled -- the whole of the",
    "'udev settled' guarantee, without a second service to express it.",
    "",
    "StartTimeout is raised to 60 because it bounds the entire start sequence,",
    "post-hook included, and settle alone may legitimately take a while on a",
    "machine with many disks. ErrorControl is Normal (0): a boot without the",
    "device manager has built-in drivers, the initramfs coldplug, and a",
    "console, which is a degraded machine rather than an unbootable one.",
    "",
    "No dependencies. The TRM's boot order puts eudev first in phase 2, before",
    "authd exists, and nothing here changes that. Networking and anything that",
    "opens a device by a stable name should Requires it.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the eudev package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an image",
    "names it in [registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\eudev",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath",          "type": "sz",    "data": "/bin/udevd" },
        { "name": "Triggers",           "type": "multi", "data": ["boot"] },
        { "name": "Identity",           "type": "sz",    "data": "SYSTEM" },
        { "name": "RequiredPrivileges", "type": "multi", "data": ["SeLoadDriverPrivilege", "SeTcbPrivilege", "SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege"] },
        { "name": "ExecStartPost",      "type": "multi", "data": ["/libexec/udev-coldplug"] },
        { "name": "StartTimeout",       "type": "dword", "data": 60 },
        { "name": "Readiness",          "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy",      "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl",       "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "DisplayName",        "type": "sz",    "data": "Device manager" },
        { "name": "Description",        "type": "sz",    "data": "udev: loads drivers for devices as they appear and maintains stable device names under /dev" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
